  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Puc 902.08 Distribution Utility",
  "priorExpiration": "2014-07-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 902.08 “Distribution Utility” means the company that owns and/or operates the distribution facilities delivering electricity to the customer-generator’s premises, and includes a rural electric cooperative for which a certificate of deregulation is on file with the commission.\n\nSource. #9515, eff 7-18-09; ss by #9998, eff 9-20-11 (from Puc 902.05); ss by #10502, INTERIM, eff 1-3-14, EXPIRED: 7-2-14 (from Puc 902.07)\n\nNew. #10757, eff 1-8-15; ss by #13080, eff 9-14-20 (formerly Puc 902.05)",
